Spread the cell loads and unloads of a grid change over the following frames (cell change hitch fix).

When the player walks across a cell border outdoors, Scene::changeCellGrid unloads the row of cells
that left the grid and loads the new row (3 cells, 5 on a diagonal), all in one frame. Measured on a
Retroid Pocket Duo Lite with the DSPerf probe and simpleperf: about 55 ms of that frame on a west
step, spread over hundreds of objects (insertCell 34 ms, unloadCell 11 ms), with no single part
worth fixing on its own. The frame after it pays the first draw of all the new objects at once.

A grid change asked for by walking (Scene::update) now only does the grid itself in its frame
(navigator bounds, terrain and paging active grid, paged refs). The new cells are then loaded one
per frame, nearest first, and the old ones unloaded one per frame after that. All of these cells are
a cell or more away from the player when this happens, past the viewing distance. A second grid
change works out what is left against its own grid; teleports, loading a game and changes to an
interior still load everything at once as before, and drop whatever was waiting.

